WHY CC BY-SA 4.0 AND NOT MIT
----------------------------
The pipeline source code would normally be released under a permissive licence.
CC BY-SA 4.0 is used for the repository as a whole because the English emotion
classifier is fine-tuned on the "super-emotion" dataset
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/cirimus/super-emotion), which is distributed
under CC BY-SA 4.0. ShareAlike propagates to derived works, so any checkpoint
trained on that data, and any distribution bundling such a checkpoint, must
carry a compatible licence.

Consequences worth knowing before you redistribute:

  - Weights trained on super-emotion inherit CC BY-SA 4.0. They cannot be
    relicensed as MIT.
  - The NLLB-200 translation models used in stage 5B are CC-BY-NC-4.0:
    non-commercial. Any commercial use of this pipeline requires replacing
    stage 5B.
  - Third-party models loaded from the Hub keep their own licences; see the
    per-model `license` field in src/vea/config.py and docs/LICENSING.md.

If you split the repository so that no CC BY-SA 4.0 data or weights are
included, the pipeline code itself can be relicensed by its authors.

REQUIRED ATTRIBUTION
--------------------
See the Citation section of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for the upstream datasets and
models that must be credited.
